[32m+[m[32m## Friends and messages[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse **Watch**, **Messages**, and **History** in the header to switch pages. The Messages page contains only messaging; the video link field, player, and notes stay on Watch. Switching pages saves progress and stops video playback.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen **Messages** in the header. Enter an existing account's username to send a friend request. The recipient can accept or decline it; the sender can cancel a pending request. Texting and attachments are available only after acceptance.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChoose a friend to open a conversation. Text supports Unicode emoji, and the smile button opens an emoji picker. New messages appear automatically (about every two seconds while the app is open). Older messages are available with **Load older messages**. Switching conversations or hiding Messages preserves unsent drafts while signed in; signing out or reloading clears drafts.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe paperclip attaches one file per message, up to **10 MB**: PDF, PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, or audio (WebM, Ogg, MP4/M4A, WAV, MP3). Review the attachment before pressing **Send**. Pictures display inline, audio has playback controls, and PDFs have a download link. File contents are checked against the selected media type; SVG and HTML are not supported.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse the microphone button to record a voice message, then the stop button to preview it before sending. Recordings stop automatically after two minutes; closing Messages stops recording and keeps its preview. Microphone access requires browser permission and a browser that supports recording. You can attach an existing audio file if recording is unavailable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMessages and the actual PDF, image, and audio **bytes are stored in SQLite**, not an external file host. Only the sender and recipient can retrieve a message's attachment through the app. Messages are not end-to-end encrypted; someone with filesystem access to the database can read them. Attachments increase database size, so keep backups of the `data` folder.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis remains a **local PC app**. Both accounts must exist on the same Stillroom server. To try two accounts at once, use a regular browser window and a private window (or separate browser profiles). Separate PCs running their own copies do not share accounts or messages. Publishing the repository to GitHub does not create a shared messaging server.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Notifications and quiet mode[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bell and Messages tab show a red count for new incoming friend requests and unread messages, with unread counts beside the relevant friends. Notifications update about every three seconds while Stillroom is open. Viewing requests marks them seen; viewing the latest messages in a visible conversation marks them read. Background polling and hidden conversations do not mark messages read.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen the **bell → Notifications** switch to turn notifications on or off. Turning them off enables **Quiet mode**: no red dots, counts, sounds, device pop-ups, or notification items. You can still open chats and respond whenever you want. This preference is stored per account in SQLite and applies across browsers connected to that same server. Unread state is retained while muted, so unread items can appear again if notifications are reenabled.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese are in-app notifications. There is no push service sending alerts while the app is closed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Mobile and installation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe interface adapts to small screens. On Messages, phones show the friends list first; select a friend to open the conversation, then use **Friends** to return. The composer adjusts to the on-screen keyboard, with safe-area space for phone notches and home indicators.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse the **install/download icon** in the header for installation instructions or an **Install app** button when Chrome makes it available:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Android Chrome:** browser ⋮ menu → Install app or Add to Home screen.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **iPhone Chrome:** Share beside the address bar → Add to Home Screen → Add. If the option is unavailable, open the same URL in Safari and use Share → Add to Home Screen.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Desktop Chrome/Edge:** the install icon in the address bar or the browser's Install app menu.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBrowser menus and installation support vary. See [Chrome's iPhone instructions](https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/9658361?co=GENIE.Platform%3DiOS) and [PWA installation requirements](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Progressive_web_apps/Guides/Making_PWAs_installable).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStillroom includes an app manifest, standalone display mode, Android/iPhone icons, and a service worker. Only public interface files are cached for an offline shell. Accounts, notes, history, messages, and attachments are never cached by the service worker. Sign-in and other features still need a connection to the running server; installation does not copy the Python server or database onto a phone.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Connecting a phone to your PC server[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**127.0.0.1 on your phone means the phone itself, not your PC.** For phone installation, Stillroom needs an HTTPS URL reachable from the phone, using a certificate trusted by that device. The default command remains private to your PC and does not make it reachable from a phone automatically.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf you already have a trusted TLS certificate and a hostname that resolves to your PC, the server supports explicit HTTPS access:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mpython3 start.py --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8765 --origin https://YOUR_HOSTNAME:8765 --cert /path/to/fullchain.pem --key /path/to/private-key.pem --no-browser[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen that exact HTTPS address on the phone. Allow the port on your firewall as needed, and keep the PC/server running. The certificate must cover `YOUR_HOSTNAME` and be trusted by the phone; bypassing a certificate warning is not a reliable installation setup. Keep certificates and private keys outside the repository (common key files and `certs/` are ignored).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlternatively, keep the Python server on loopback behind an HTTPS reverse proxy that forwards all paths to `127.0.0.1:8765`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mpython3 start.py --origin https://YOUR_HOSTNAME --no-browser[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mConfigure that proxy and its trusted certificate separately. `--origin` must match the exact address users open, including a nondefault port. HTTPS sessions use Secure cookies. This task prepares the app and server for phone installation; it does not provision a domain, certificate, proxy, or public deployment.[m
[32m+[m
 ## Database and privacy[m
 [m
[31m-The database is created automatically at `data/stillroom.sqlite3`. It stores account records, hashed passwords, sessions, notes, history, and progress. Passwords use salted scrypt hashing; session cookies are HttpOnly and SameSite=Strict. Account APIs require an active session, and the server does not serve the database or source files over HTTP.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe database is created automatically at `data/stillroom.sqlite3`. It stores account records, hashed passwords, sessions, notes, history, progress, friendships, messages, attachment BLOBs, notification settings, and read markers. Passwords use salted scrypt hashing; session cookies are HttpOnly and SameSite=Strict. Account APIs require an active session, and the server does not serve the database or source files over HTTP.[m
 [m
[31m-Back up the `data` folder while the server is stopped to preserve accounts and notes. Clearing browser storage does not delete database notes. The server listens only on `127.0.0.1`; this is a local PC application, not a public hosting setup. Anyone with filesystem access to the database can read its notes and history. The app has no analytics. Loading videos connects your browser to the chosen provider.[m
[32m+[m[32mBack up the `data` folder while the server is stopped to preserve accounts and notes. Clearing browser storage does not delete database notes. By default the server listens only on `127.0.0.1`. Network access requires explicit HTTPS configuration as described above. Anyone with filesystem access to the database can read its notes and history. The app has no analytics. Loading videos connects your browser to the chosen provider.[m
